	'k101ce9b5' => 'Morning light enters through tall windows, illuminating timber floorboards and linen curtains. In the apartment kitchen, coffee brews on the induction cooktop while bread brought from the neighbourhood bakery rests on the counter. Outside on the quiet pavement, neighbours walk toward the morning tram stop. Inside the corridors of Ashgrove House, Canal Row, and Linden Court, a restful quiet prevails. Residents begin their day without hurry, whether sitting at their dedicated timber work desk to plan the day ahead or preparing for an early morning walk through the nearby city park before meetings begin.',
	'k10a84262' => 'As dusk descends across Calder Harbour, residents return home from assignments across the city. The tram brings engineers, researchers, and professionals back to their neighbourhood, just a short walk from their front door. Residents greet the house manager at the front desk before heading upstairs to their apartment. Weekly linen deliveries have been completed, leaving bedrooms refreshed and organized. Table lamps are switched on, casting a warm glow across sofas and bookshelves. In the shared laundry room and along the quiet hallways, the building settles into a comfortable, familiar domestic evening.',
